{"beat": 20, "name": "HOW TO HOLD A PRICE", "text": "So how do you hold a price when everything under it costs more? A book on chain stores from 1922 described exactly how: Woolworth clung to the old policy by decreasing the units. The size was made smaller, less candy was sold for ten cents, matches which had been one cent a box were five cents; things were sold separately, one stocking for ten cents, the pail ten cents and the cover ten. Look at the stocking. A pair became one. The price on the tag never moved. What the customer got for it did. Your customers have a name for that today, and it isn't a kind one.", "provider": "placeholder", "words": [{"word": "So", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.16}, {"word": "how", "start": 0.16, "end": 0.36}, {"word": "do", "start": 0.36, "end": 0.48}, {"word": "you", "start": 0.48, "end": 0.58}, {"word": "hold", "start": 0.58, "end": 0.86}, {"word": "a", "start": 0.86, "end": 1.02}, {"word": "price", "start": 1.02, "end": 1.36}, {"word": "when", "start": 1.36, "end": 1.6}, {"word": "everything", "start": 1.6, "end": 2.12}, {"word": "under", "start": 2.12, "end": 2.42}, {"word": "it", "start": 2.42, "end": 2.56}, {"word": "costs", "start": 2.56, "end": 2.82}, {"word": "more?", "start": 2.82, "end": 3.24}, {"word": "A", "start": 3.94, "end": 4.04}, {"word": "book", "start": 4.04, "end": 4.22}, {"word": "on", "start": 4.22, "end": 4.42}, {"word": "chain", "start": 4.42, "end": 4.8}, {"word": "stores", "start": 4.8, "end": 5.36}, {"word": "from", "start": 5.36, "end": 5.66}, {"word": "1922", "start": 5.66, "end": 6.72}, {"word": "described", "start": 6.72, "end": 7.44}, {"word": "exactly", "start": 7.44, "end": 8.24}, {"word": "how:", "start": 8.24, "end": 8.64}, {"word": "Woolworth", "start": 9.38, "end": 9.78}, {"word": "clung", "start": 9.78, "end": 10.2}, {"word": "to", "start": 10.2, "end": 10.38}, {"word": "the", "start": 10.38, "end": 10.5}, {"word": "old", "start": 10.5, "end": 10.72}, {"word": "policy", "start": 10.72, "end": 11.26